    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0242" n="110" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Leahy Papers Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 80 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commanding General, United States Military Mission
                        in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Deane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Supreme Commander, Allied Expeditionary Force</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Eisenhower</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-20">20 June 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>To ETOUSA Forward for Eisenhower and AGWar for General
                    Marshall’s eyes only from
                        Deane
                    top sec
                    MX 24738.</p>
                <p>
                    Antonov informed me this morning that
                    the question of advanced preparations in Berlin for the forthcoming conference
                    was a matter that was being decided between our governments, indicating that he
                    could not change his former decision to postpone General Parks reconnaissance until after Zhukov got back to Berlin on about 28 or 29
                    June. Harriman has already taken this
                    question up twice with the Foreign Office, once on 15 June<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d80-f1"/> when the original request was received to have General Parks authorized to go to Berlin and
                    again last night<anchor n="2" xml:id="d80-f2"/> upon receipt of ETOUSA
                    Fwd
                    S 91539.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d80-f3"/> We shall
                    continue our efforts to arrange for General
                        Parks reconnaissance.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
